  "raw_text": "Step 1: Substitute \\(a = 9\\) and \\(b = 2\\) into the given operation definition \\(a \\& b = \\frac{\\sqrt{ab + a}}{\\sqrt{ab - b}}\\).\n\nStep 2: Calculate the numerator \\(\\sqrt{ab + a}\\):\n\\[ ab + a = 9 \\cdot 2 + 9 = 18 + 9 = 27 \\]\nSo, the numerator becomes \\(\\sqrt{27}\\).\n\nStep 3: Calculate the denominator \\(\\sqrt{ab - b}\\):\n\\[ ab - b = 9 \\cdot 2 - 2 = 18 - 2 = 16 \\]\nSo, the denominator becomes \\(\\sqrt{16}\\).\n\nStep 4: Simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{\\sqrt{16}}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{\\sqrt{16}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{4} \\]\n\nStep 5: Simplify \\(\\sqrt{27}\\) to its simplest radical form:\n\\[ \\sqrt{27} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 3} = \\sqrt{9} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 3\\sqrt{3} \\]\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}}\\)<|im_end|>",
